                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1700" notBefore="1600">
                        <p>17th century?, <placeName key="place_1000070">French</placeName> or <placeName key="place_7024097">Flemish</placeName>?: thin pasteboards; 
                           polished red leather, elaborate all-over gilt tooling on covers and outside edges but central oval on each cover left unfilled (for coat of arms?); 
                           spine flat, with similar gilt tooling but no title; traces of two clasps, roughly removed; edges gilt, not gauffered, done after some trimming 
                           (slightly cropping the illuminated borders). Fragments of <persName role="fmo" key="person_308770014">Jacopo Soranzo’s</persName> decorative label, 
                           18th century, at top of spine
                        </p>
                           
